{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "LTX VFX: Ingredients (IC-LoRA Ingredients 0.9)",
    "description": "Core ComfyUI nodes only (LTX-2.5 support in ComfyUI core). Distilled LTX-2.5 22B (int8), 8 fixed sigmas, euler_ancestral, cfg 1 (LTXVDualCFGGuider 1/1). IC-LoRA: LoraLoaderModelOnly (strength 1.4, card default) -> GetICLoRAParameters -> LTXVAddGuide(reference sheet, frame_idx 0, strength 1) at native resolution (reference downscale factor 1), LTXVCropGuides drops the guide frames before decoding. The reference sheet is one clean panel per element (character face close-up / turnaround, prop, location) on black with no text: up to four ingredient images are stitched on black (ImageStitch: 1 as is, 2 side by side, 3 in a row, 4 as a 2x2 grid), letterboxed on black to the output size (ResizeAndPadImage) and repeated into a static clip as long as the output (RepeatImageBatch, 121 frames). Bigger panels carry more detail. Trained at 768x448 (448x768 portrait), 121 frames at 24 fps. Prompt in two parts: 'Reference sheet: <panels>' then 'Generated video: <action>'. No trigger word. The card's dev-model settings (30 steps, cfg 4) are not used: this pack runs the distilled model as the official ComfyUI template does. Generated audio kept. LTX-2 Community License (ltx-2.x-community-license, gated on Hugging Face)."
  },
